      {
        "id": 253136,
        "name": "Chief Lackey Rich",
        "username": "Chief_Lackey_Rich",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2023-07-10T13:02:53.039Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I mean, that’s true of every fictional character ever.  Even the ones who can break the Fourth Wall and directly threaten their creator with bodily harm to ensure they get their way are only able to do so with authorial permission, no matter what Guise or Deadpool may think.  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\"></p>\n<p>As for detectives, if we’re limiting it to people who actually work at it for a living, Ralph Dibny (who actually had a PI license at some points) and Detective Chimp both get to lord it over that Wayne dilettante.  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\"></p>",
